plan_in_issue:
**Goal.** A ladder bot concedes only at the start of its own turn, and only when its opponent has a lethal showing on the board that nothing the bot does this turn can stop. The opponent's hand and face-down cards never count toward that lethal. Both turns are played through the engine to prove it. If there is any doubt (the node budget runs out, the clock runs out, or a step fails), the bot plays on. Every bot follows this rule. The bot's fitted temper (`BOT_CONCEDE_FIT.share`) still decides whether it is a bot that concedes at all. A bot may also offer a draw at the start of its turn while it is clearly behind, at a small chance, within R36's limits. Two new rulings, R2660000 (concession) and R2660001 (draw offer), amend R639000, R1452, R188 and §9.12.

